{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1544","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1544","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1544\",\"parent_revision\":\"ecc482802a4714f9f9f623c996b7a64ed745c8e87c28b6db2ad9d8d622bcb5c2\",\"root_revision\":\"ecc482802a4714f9f9f623c996b7a64ed745c8e87c28b6db2ad9d8d622bcb5c2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ncheck_live_validation() in live_validation_step.py calls subprocess.run(..., timeout=_COMMAND_TIMEOUT) but does not catch subprocess.TimeoutExpired. When a live validation command exceeds the timeout, the exception propagates uncaught to the feature-verifier caller instead of returning a structured LiveValidationOutcome. Fix: catch TimeoutExpired, return structured outcome, add test for timeout scenario.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `check_live_validation()` calls `subprocess.run(..., timeout=_COMMAND_TIMEOUT)` \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py:101-108` \u2014 `subprocess.run(live_val, shell=True, ..., timeout=_COMMAND_TIMEOUT, check=False)`\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` is NOT caught \u2014 Evidence: `live_validation_step.py:82-114` \u2014 only `(FileNotFoundError, ManifestValidationError)` are caught at manifest-load time; no exception handler wraps the `subprocess.run` call at line 101\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `_COMMAND_TIMEOUT = 120` is the timeout value \u2014 Evidence: `live_validation_step.py:32`\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `LiveValidationOutcome` is the structured return type \u2014 Evidence: `live_validation_step.py:45-54` \u2014 dataclass with fields `result`, `gap_message`, `command`, `exit_code`, `stdout`, `stderr`\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** Existing test file covers 8 scenarios but NO timeout scenario \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py:63-213` \u2014 tests cover PASS, GAPS_FOUND, DEFERRED_BROWSER, DEFERRED_SKILL, SKIPPED, gap_message text, path constant, and manifest read path; no test for `TimeoutExpired`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: **missing-guardrail**\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis (5-whys):\\n1. Why does `TimeoutExpired` propagate uncaught? \u2014 The `subprocess.run` call at line 101 has no surrounding try/except.\\n2. Why was no try/except added? \u2014 The initial implementation handled only manifest-load errors; the subprocess path was treated as always-terminating.\\n3. Why was timeout not paired with error handling? \u2014 `timeout=` was set as a safety cap but `subprocess.run` raises `TimeoutExpired` (not a return-code) when it fires; that distinction was not modelled.\\n4. Why was this not caught by tests? \u2014 The test suite mocks subprocess results via `tmp_path` commands (`echo ok`, `false`) which complete immediately; no slow-command test exists.\\n5. Why did review not catch it? \u2014 The code-reviewer flagged it in T1 of P1526 and produced this issue \u2014 the review did catch it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py:100-114` \u2014 `subprocess.run` call that needs TimeoutExpired handler\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py` \u2014 add timeout test here\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSeverity: **Medium**\\n\\n- Any project whose live-validation command hangs or takes longer than 120 seconds causes an unhandled exception that crashes the feature-verifier agent's Step 8 instead of reporting a structured gap.\\n- The caller receives a traceback rather than a `LiveValidationOutcome`, breaking the Step 8 protocol contract.\\n- Affects any manifest that declares a slow or hanging `live_validation` command.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFollow-up to **P1526** (live-validation-manifest-v2). Independent of #1545 \u2014 both are P1526 quality-gate follow-ups but address different defects; can be worked in parallel.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: **XS**\\nReasoning: One narrow try/except wrapping ~14 lines of existing code, one new test function (mock-based, ~15 lines). No design decisions required \u2014 return type and field values are fully specified above.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```python\\n# Reproduce: write a manifest with a long-running live_validation command,\\n# then call check_live_validation() with _COMMAND_TIMEOUT overridden to 1 second.\\n# Expected (current): subprocess.TimeoutExpired propagates uncaught.\\n# Expected (after fix): LiveValidationOutcome(result=GAPS_FOUND, ...) returned.\\n\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\\nimport subprocess\\nimport pytest\\n\\ndef test_timeout_raises_uncaught(tmp_path):\\n    # Arrange: write a manifest that would run 'sleep 300'\\n    # Patch _COMMAND_TIMEOUT to 1 to avoid waiting\\n    # This test currently FAILS (raises TimeoutExpired instead of returning outcome)\\n    ...\\n```\\n\\nWrite a manifest with `live_validation: 'sleep 300'`, patch `_COMMAND_TIMEOUT` to `1`, call `check_live_validation(tmp_path)` \u2014 currently raises `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` uncaught.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **handle subprocess.timeoutexpired in check_live_validation** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality gate follow-up from P1526 (live-validation-manifest-v2) \u2014 code-reviewer T1\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/.dh/projects/-home-ubuntulinuxqa2-repos-claude_skills/plan/P1528-live-validation-manifest-v2-followup-1.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-05T05:48:58Z |\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria Groomed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `check_live_validation()` catches `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` specifically \u2014 NOT `Exception` or `BaseException`\\n- [ ] On timeout, returns `LiveValidationOutcome(result=LiveValidationResult.GAPS_FOUND, command=live_val, gap_message=<descriptive timeout message>)` \u2014 NOT a dict or Any\\n- [ ] `exit_code` field is `None` in the timeout outcome (no exit code available from a timed-out process)\\n- [ ] `stdout` and `stderr` are empty strings in the timeout outcome (process was killed, no output captured)\\n- [ ] A new test `test_timeout_returns_gaps_found` in `test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py` patches `subprocess.run` to raise `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` and asserts the returned outcome has `result == GAPS_FOUND` and `gap_message` is not None\\n- [ ] No bare `except Exception` or `except BaseException` is introduced \u2014 rule BLE001 must not be suppressed\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py` exits 0\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4db34fee6389b93149a67332652839eb928580c4788677989136ed4e4110e224\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWDFyA\"}"}